From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: ubi: allow skipping bootloader-requested auto-attachment

An initramfs may be loaded by U-Boot while inheriting ubi.mtd=rootfs from
the persistent vendor boot path. When NAND becomes visible, UBI's built-in
late init then scans the entire vendor rootfs before the initramfs can
start. The Acer Wave 7 test boot spent over 119 seconds in UBI attach
with QPIC ECC errors, preventing user-space networking and activating
the timed recovery.

Provide a generic read-only no_autoattach parameter. It skips only
automatic attachment during UBI init, including explicit ubi.mtd=
requests; user-space can still attach MTD devices deliberately via
ubiattach after initialization. Default behavior is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>

---
diff --git a/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c b/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c
--- a/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c
@@ -71,6 +71,9 @@
 
 /* MTD devices specification parameters */
 static struct mtd_dev_param mtd_dev_param[UBI_MAX_DEVICES];
+
+/* Allow an initramfs to ignore stale ubi.mtd= bootloader parameters. */
+static bool no_autoattach;
 #ifdef CONFIG_MTD_UBI_FASTMAP
 /* UBI module parameter to enable fastmap automatically on non-fastmap images */
 static bool fm_autoconvert;
@@ -1342,6 +1345,11 @@
 {
 	int err, i, k;
 
+	if (no_autoattach) {
+		pr_info("UBI: automatic MTD attachment disabled by parameter\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	/* Attach MTD devices */
 	for (i = 0; i < mtd_devs; i++) {
 		struct mtd_dev_param *p = &mtd_dev_param[i];
@@ -1653,6 +1661,10 @@
 	mtd_devs += 1;
 	return 0;
 }
+
+module_param_named(no_autoattach, no_autoattach, bool, 0400);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(no_autoattach,
+	"Disable all boot-time UBI MTD attachments, including ubi.mtd=; manual ubiattach remains available.");
 
 module_param_call(mtd, ubi_mtd_param_parse, NULL, NULL, 0400);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(mtd, "MTD devices to attach. Parameter format: mtd=<name|num|path>[,<vid_hdr_offs>[,max_beb_per1024[,ubi_num[,enable_fm[,need_resv_pool]]]]].\n"
